# Phase 4 continuation — implementation and validation update
- Resumed on clean branch after previous feature commits. Continued source-backed audit of Java 5.5.1.
- Verified actual client call sites for BATCH_ACK_MESSAGE, QUERY_ASSIGNMENT, SET_MESSAGE_REQUEST_MODE, and LITE_SUBSCRIPTION_CTL; implemented corresponding body models. Implemented Java compact BatchAck names and Base64 BitSet encoding.
- Added Java fixtures for transaction/reply/runtime headers and additional POP/Lite headers. Added Rust body fixtures for assignment, request-mode, Lite subscription, BatchAck, reset-offset, consumer status, and direct consume; Java verifier decodes 19 Rust header frames and 7 body frames and checks selected fields.
- Added body models/tests for source-shaped reset/status queue maps; Java uses a Fastjson extension with MessageQueue object keys (not strict JSON), so tests parse the pinned fixture shape and verify queue/offset values rather than claim strict serde_json validity of Java's non-standard map syntax.
- Updated REQUEST_CODES.md to separate implemented models from remaining fixture/coverage gaps.
- Validation passed: workspace tests (common 11, protocol 22 unit + 7 headers integration + 1 fixture integration, remoting 50 unit + 77 transport); workspace Clippy with `-D warnings`; fmt check; Maven verify (Java oracle/self-test + 17 manifest scenarios + Java decode of 19 Rust headers and 7 body frames); workspace metadata check; differential self-test.
- Remaining Phase 4 blockers: not every listed header/model has Java→Rust and Rust→Java fixture assertions; request/response body field parity not exhaustive; Lite ACK/unsubscribe models and further source-mapped optional families remain; header negative/boolean/overflow table is not exhaustive; P4-V01/V02/V03 therefore remain unchecked. Phase 4 is not complete.
- Commits for this continuation pending, split into fixtures/verifier, tests/models as appropriate, and docs/log.
- Updated operation matrix: implemented models are distinguished from missing Lite ACK/unsubscribe and from incomplete exhaustive fixture/negative-case coverage. Documented the specific Fastjson MessageQueue-key extension mismatch in reset/status body JSON; it remains a protocol interoperability blocker, not an accepted difference.
- Final workspace validation for this continuation passed: workspace cargo tests, fmt, Clippy, Java Maven verify (19 Rust header frames and 7 Rust body frames decoded), metadata check, differential self-test, and diff check.
- Phase 4 remains incomplete. P4-V01/V02/V03 cannot be marked complete until every implemented header/body has both-direction Oracle evidence, exhaustive invalid/missing-field coverage, and JSON wire semantic parity is resolved.
- Preparing separate commits for verifier/fixture generator, Rust fixture assertions, and compatibility status/log.
- Implemented `ResetOffsetBody::encode_java_json` and `GetConsumerStatusBody::encode_java_json` for Java Fastjson's non-standard MessageQueue object-key form; kept standard Serde serialization separate. Tests parse Java fixture queue keys and assert Java-compatible encoder bytes exactly.
- Corrected direct-consume body result model to Java `CMResult` enum values (`CR_SUCCESS`, etc.) and fixture test checks semantic JSON (object key order is not treated as semantic).
- Final targeted validation: full workspace tests passed (common 11, protocol 22 unit + 7 header/body integration + fixture integration, remoting 50 unit + 77 transport); workspace Clippy, fmt, workspace metadata, differential self-test, Maven verify passed. Maven decoded 19 Rust headers and 7 Rust typed bodies.
- Commits created: `b80de0b test(protocol): expand Java typed fixture round trips`, `3bac596 test(protocol): cover typed body and header oracle cases`, `4d3b???` Java queue-key adapter (see Git history), plus compatibility and log commits.
